    <section id="m01-course-fundamentals-and-net-overview-01" class="mb-5">
        <h2>Course Fundamentals &amp; .NET Overview</h2>
        <p class="zoomable">This course keeps every explanation short and friendly so you never feel lost.</p>
        <p class="zoomable">You will meet the <span class="tt" data-tip="Microsoft's open-source framework that hosts languages like C# and manages runtime services">.NET</span> platform before touching code.</p>
        <p class="zoomable">We focus on how projects flow from idea to a running app in small steps.</p>
        <p class="zoomable">You will see the parts that do the heavy lifting, like libraries and runtime helpers.</p>
        <p class="zoomable">By the end of this section, you can explain the big picture to a teammate in one minute.</p>
        <p class="text-success fw-semibold zoomable"><strong>Why this matters?</strong> A clear map prevents overwhelm and shows how each lesson fits the final app.</p>

        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded zoomable">Idea --> .NET runtime --> Libraries --> Your App --> Users</pre>

        <figure class="zoomable text-center">
            <svg width="320" height="140" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label=".NET overview diagram">
