        </figure>

        <div class="p-3 example-box rounded zoomable">
            <strong>Example:</strong> A to-do list web app uses .NET libraries to manage dates, save items, and show them on a page.
        </div>

        <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded zoomable"><code>// A friendly welcome in C#
Console.WriteLine("Welcome to C# New!");
Console.WriteLine(".NET will handle memory and safety while you learn logic.");</code></pre>

        <p class="zoomable"><strong>Real-world use case:</strong> Explaining how a business dashboard sits on .NET helps stakeholders trust the tech choice.</p>
        <p class="zoomable"><strong>Beginner tip:</strong> Think of .NET as a supportive platform that cleans up chores like memory and security.</p>
        <p class="zoomable"><strong>Advanced note:</strong> Different flavors like .NET Framework, .NET Core, and .NET 8 share many APIs but target different environments.</p>

        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-3">
