    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2>FAQs</h2>
        <ul class="zoomable">
            <li><strong>Do I need Windows?</strong> No, .NET runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux.</li>
            <li><strong>Is Visual Studio Code enough?</strong> Yes, but Visual Studio has more guided templates.</li>
            <li><strong>How do I fix missing SDK?</strong> Install the latest .NET SDK from the official site once per machine.</li>
            <li><strong>Can I skip CLI?</strong> You can, but learning a few commands speeds every project.</li>
            <li><strong>Where are samples stored?</strong> In the project folder created by the CLI or IDE.</li>
            <li><strong>Is C# good for web?</strong> Yes, it powers ASP.NET Core for APIs and web apps.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

